      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I have a clear picture of the test. Let me write the improved version with better readability — clearer variable names, descriptive assertion messages, and an explanatory comment about the non-obvious \"FALSE\" timezone fallback.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version uses descriptive variable names (`scalarShape`, `frenchLocale`, `unknownTimeZone`, `noFeatures`, `lenient`, `formatValue`), adds a comment explaining the non-obvious GMT fallback for the \"FALSE\" timezone ID, and groups assertions with brief explanations of what each one verifies — all while preserving identical runtime behavior."
    }
